{"name":"Australia Medicare Statistics: MBS item reports for genomic and whole-genome/exome items (73358, 73359, 73360, plus later rare-disease WGS and cancer-panel items)","url":"https://medicarestatistics.humanservices.gov.au/statistics/mbs_item.html","access":"Public form, no login. Enter item numbers 73358, 73359, 73360 and any other MBS genomic items found on MBS Online (search mbsonline.gov.au for 'whole genome' and 'whole exome'). Select monthly or financial-year services and benefits for Jan 2019 to Sep 2026. The portal maps renumbered items. Also try the data.gov.au 'MBS group' dataset (https://www.data.gov.au/data/dataset/medicare-benefits-schedule-mbs-group) for bulk CSV. Precedent: MSAC used this portal for items 73339/73340 and found uptake of only 15% and 4% of forecast.","labels":["1C"],"rationale":"These are national, claims-based counts of clinical genome and exome tests with a monthly time series up to 2026. They do not depend on what any company says. If WGS and exome claims are flat or growing in the low teens, that is hard evidence that clinical WGS is ramping slowly. The MSAC actual-versus-predicted gap is a ready-made framing for 'too small, too slow.' This is a new country and dataset for the corpus.","expected_payoff":"high"},
{"name":"CMS Part B National Summary Data File (formerly BESS), 2024 and 2025 files: allowed services by PLA code for MRD (0340U Signatera, Reveal, clonoSEQ 0364U, NeXT Personal, RaDaR, Oncodetect) and 81425/81426 genome codes","url":"https://www.cms.gov/data-research/statistics-trends-and-reports/part-b-national-summary-data-file","access":"Public download. There is an AMA click-through licence page but no account or login. Download the latest annual zip (the page showed a file dated 13 Mar 2026; the 2025 file may now be posted). Open the 0000U-range data set, then pull allowed services and allowed charges for 0340U, other MRD PLA codes, 81425–81427 and 0094U (rapid WGS). Compare year on year from 2022 to 2025. Avoid S748 and S527, which are the provider-level files.","labels":["1C"],"rationale":"This gives national Medicare fee-for-service counts of MRD draws and genome tests, which are independent of company releases. Comparing Medicare 0340U services with the MRD volumes Natera reports shows the Medicare mix and whether Medicare MRD growth is slowing. Genome-code services show how small clinical WGS is in absolute numbers. A strong year would count against the thesis.","expected_payoff":"high"},
