{"name":"Germany Modellvorhaben Genomsequenzierung (§64e SGB V, genomDE): case counts for clinical WGS in rare disease and oncology since July 2024","url":"https://www.gkv-spitzenverband.de/krankenversicherung/forschung_modellvorhaben/mv_genomsequenzierung/genomsequenzierung.jsp","access":"Open HTML, no login. Read the GKV-Spitzenverband page for evaluation or annual reports. Then search bfarm.de for 'Modellvorhaben Genomsequenzierung Fallzahlen' or 'Jahresbericht', and the genomDE BMG page (https://www.bundesgesundheitsministerium.de/themen/gesundheitswesen/personalisierte-medizin/genomde-de.html). Also check TMF symposium slides (e.g. https://www.tmf-ev.de/sites/default/files/2026-06/...) and the ACHSE NAKSE 2025 posters for enrolled-case numbers. Compare the original 'Fallzahlenabschätzung' with actual numbers.","labels":["1C"],"rationale":"This is Europe's largest new reimbursed clinical WGS program, with more than 20 university hospitals. If actual cases in the first two years are a few thousand against a plan of tens of thousands, that is independent evidence that clinical WGS ramps slower than planned even when it is funded. The planned-versus-actual comparison is directly quotable.","expected_payoff":"medium"},
